{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104947","id":2435504988,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6RKttc","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104947","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104947.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104947.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104947","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104947/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104947/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104947/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/50ab06d73ea054df632c0a8369914be38352d548","number":104947,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[3.x] Change ARVR Nodes default interpolation to off","user":{"login":"Asaduji","id":39374509,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5Mzc0NTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39374509?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asaduji","html_url":"https://github.com/Asaduji","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asaduji/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asaduji/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asaduji/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asaduji/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asaduji/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asaduji/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asaduji/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asaduji/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asaduji/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Follow up for https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103685\r\nAddresses the second issue mentioned here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103685#issuecomment-2718336903\r\n\r\nARVR Nodes get their transform updated on `NOTIFICATION_INTERNAL_PROCESS` , this causes some issues if interpolation is enabled, this PR fixes:\r\n- `ARVRCamera`, `ARVRController` and  `ARVRAnchor` jitter when interpolation is enabled in project settings.\r\n- Fixes the warning `Interpolated Camera triggered from outside physics process`.\r\nThanks to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103685 we can now have mixed interpolation modes on the scene without issues, so interpolation on ARVR Nodes should be disabled by default.\r\n\r\n`ARVROrigin` isn't affected by this because its transform isn't updated on `NOTIFICATION_INTERNAL_PROCESS`.\r\n\r\nHere is an comparison running at 10 physics FPS:\r\n\r\nBefore\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c72a63b3-2838-4ed7-a5d1-f81371ecca88\r\n\r\nAfter\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a0b9c775-7ad8-4af4-90fd-6bee86d1d991\r\n\r\nIt's a bit hard to notice without a VR headset.\r\n\r\nThe alternative would be to change the transform on `NOTIFICATION_INTERNAL_PHYSICS_PROCESS` if interpolation is enabled on the nodes, it would also fix the issue but it would introduce pretty severe input lag for the tracking. \r\nIn my opinion these nodes just shouldn't be interpolated at all, users will want the latest tracking data available on any situation.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":865585000,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NjU1ODUwMDA=","url":"https://api.github.